#* {{quote-book|en|author=Elliot B. Koffman|title=Pascal: Problem Solving and Program Design|year=1989|publisher=Addison-Wesley|page=406|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=dBUiAQAAIAAJ&q=%22record%22+pascal&dq=%22record%22+pascal&hl=&cd=3&source=gbs_api|isbn=978-0-201-11834-6|passage=This chapter examines another data structure, the '''record''' (available in Pascal but not in all other high-level languages). '''Records''' make it easier to organize and represent information in Pascal, a major reason for the popularity of the Pascal{{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Ian F. Darwin|title=Java Cookbook|year=2020|publisher=O'Reilly Media|page=232|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=H9PXDwAAQBAJ&pg=PA232&dq=%22record%22+type+Java&hl=&cd=9&source=gbs_api#v=onepage&q=%22record%22%20type%20Java&f=false|isbn=978-1-4920-7255-3|passage=The new '''record''' type provides another solution. A '''record''' is a class-like construct for data classes, a restricted form of class like enums and annotations.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Joseph Albahari|title=C# 9.0 in a Nutshell|year=2021|publisher=O'Reilly Media|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=uUwgEAAAQBAJ&pg=PA210&dq=%22record%22+C#&hl=&cd=15&source=gbs_api#v=onepage&q=%22record%22%20C#&f=false|isbn=978-1-0981-0093-3|page=210|passage=A '''record''' is a special kind of class that's designed to work well with immutable (readonly) data.}}
